! pp_dijet_asym_floor.cmnd — pp_dijet.cmnd with an ASYMMETRIC k_t floor: the
! persisted x/y sequences keep the 1 GeV perturbative floor, while the aux
! (conditioning-side) traversal groomes off-spine branches down to 0.2 GeV.
!
!   ./pythia_driver 100000 jets_asym.root 1 cpp/cards/pp_dijet_asym_floor.cmnd
!
! WHY. `SoftDrop:ktFloor` does two jobs. On the sequences it scopes the PREDICTED and
! matched object to the band where hadron<->parton correspondence holds — that job is
! non-negotiable. The aux scalars are hadron-level CONDITIONING inputs, never targets,
! and nothing requires those to sit in the perturbative band (`jet_pt` and `|eta|`
! already do not). Meanwhile a fixed ABSOLUTE floor cuts far deeper off-spine, because
! a secondary plane hangs off a prong carrying only z*pT of the jet: at 1 GeV, 80.6%
! of jets have NO passing off-spine splitting, so `x_nsec` is a near-binary variable
! that is zero four times out of five. Dropping the off-spine floor to 0.2 GeV takes
! <n_sec> from 0.25 to 2.31 and the zero fraction from 80.6% to 18.2%, while the
! targets — the y sequences — are left exactly as the symmetric card produces them.
!
! WHAT IT COSTS. A looser floor buys information and buys hadronization sensitivity.
! Validate with the generator systematic (configs/experiment/pythia_vs_herwig.yaml),
! not with the NLL alone. And note `x_mg`/`x_ptg` are redefined by this card: their
! documented job is to be the complement of the recorded sequence ("how much did THIS
! grooming remove"), and under an asymmetric floor they are the complement of a tree
! the model never sees. Treat them as distinct features from the symmetric ones —
! the `kt_floor_sec` provenance column is what makes the difference detectable.
!
! See docs/PLAN_Input.md ("Asymmetric k_t floors") and cpp/include/lund_io.hpp.

! ---- generator (standard PYTHIA settings) --------------------------------
Beams:eCM            = 13000.
HardQCD:all          = on
PhaseSpace:pTHatMin  = 100.
PartonLevel:MPI      = off          ! pure hadronization study (no underlying event)
Print:quiet          = on
Random:setSeed       = on
Random:seed          = 1            ! overridden by the CLI seed argument if given

! ---- jet finding / matching (custom; anti-kt + greedy one-to-one) --------
HadronJet:R          = 0.4          ! anti-kt jet radius
HadronJet:ptMin      = 20.          ! GeV; min jet pt at both levels
HadronJet:maxRap     = 2.0          ! |y| acceptance on the hadron jet
HadronJet:matchdR    = 0.3          ! hadron<->parton matching cone

! ---- grooming (custom; Soft Drop boundary + perturbative floor) ----------
SoftDrop:zCut        = 0.1          ! CMS/ATLAS standard
SoftDrop:beta        = 0.0          ! 0 = mMDT-like, most NP-robust
SoftDrop:R0          = 1.0          ! angular normalisation (drops out for beta=0)
SoftDrop:ktFloor     = 1.0          ! GeV; SPINE floor -> governs the x/y sequences
SoftDrop:ktFloorSec  = 0.2          ! GeV; OFF-SPINE floor -> aux traversal only.
                                    ! <= 0 (the default) mirrors ktFloor, i.e. the
                                    ! single-floor behaviour of pp_dijet.cmnd.

! ---- provenance tag stamped per entry ------------------------------------
Analysis:generatorTag = PYTHIA-8.3:tune-Monash
